  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have NNN sticks of length 1,2,...,N1, 2, ..., N1,2,...,N respectively.\n\nCan you make a non-degenerate triangle†^{\\dagger}† with some 333 sticks out of these NNN sticks? Find the maximum possible perimeter‡^{\\ddagger}‡ of a triangle you can make, or print −1-1−1 if not possible.\n\n†^{\\dagger}† You can make a non-degenerate triangle with sticks of sizes AAA, BBB and CCC if and only if 2⋅max⁡(A,B,C)&lt;A+B+C2 \\cdot \\max(A, B, C) &lt; A + B + C2⋅max(A,B,C)&lt;A+B+C.\n\n‡^{\\ddagger}‡ The perimeter of a triangle made with sticks of lengths AAA, BBB and CCC is A+B+CA + B + CA+B+C.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input contains NNN - the number of sticks.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the maximum perimeter or −1-1−1 if not possible.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "3≤N≤1083 \\le N \\le 10^83≤N≤108"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n3",
        "output": "9\n-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : You can make a triangle with the sticks of sies 444, 333 and 222. This has the maximum perimeter possible of 4+3+2=94 + 3 + 2 = 94+3+2=9.\nTest Case 2 : No triangle is possible."
      }
    ]
  },
